1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,960
A hiker found the body of a faceless girl.

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:04,640
Emma has that top.

3
00:00:04,760 --> 00:00:06,600
There's no match on her fingerprints.

4
00:00:06,680 --> 00:00:08,160
Probably someone without an ID card

5
00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:11,080
but somehow managed to live in Hong Kong.

6
00:00:11,240 --> 00:00:13,040
Something must have happened to Emma.

7
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:15,720
See? Emma just texted me. She's OK.

8
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:17,560
Don't worry, your sister is fine.

9
00:00:17,640 --> 00:00:18,520
I'll take you to her.

10
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:27,640
(Day 7 after Emma left)

11
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:30,760
What's wrong?

12
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:31,760
What is it?

13
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:32,720
Look at this!

14
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:34,800
Female corpse found in the New Territories.

15
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:37,440
Bodies found by hikers is nothing new.

16
00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:39,120
But this time the victim's face

17
00:01:39,280 --> 00:01:40,920
was chewed up by wild boars

18
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:42,120
leaving behind a bloody mess.

19
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:43,440
It was a faceless corpse.

20
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:45,160
She has the same build as Emma.

21
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:48,440
Emma has the same top. It's Emma!

22
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:51,880
(Faceless female body found in woods)

23
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,200
(Police conducting investigation)

24
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:54,960
Wait...no, calm down.

25
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:59,280
This footage is dark and blurry.

26
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:02,680
It also says the face of the corpse

27
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:04,840
was chewed up by wild boars.

28
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:05,960
You can't tell who it was.

29
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:07,600
How can we be sure it was Emma?

30
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:10,040
Daddy, I recognize the top.

31
00:02:10,160 --> 00:02:11,960
I bought it with Emma the other day.

32
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:13,840
I really think it was her.

33
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:15,880
That top is dirty.

34
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:18,760
A lot of people have tops like that.

35
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:20,720
No...it can't be her.

36
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:22,440
Even if that wasn't Emma,

37
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:24,560
I'm sure she's in trouble.

38
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:27,280
She's been missing for so long,

39
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:28,600
I think we should call the Police.

40
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:31,680
Are you crazy? We can't.

41
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:34,120
Your sister ran away on her own.

42
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:36,000
She's not missing.

43
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:40,120
Besides, you don't have ID cards.

44
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:41,080
If we could call the Police,

45
00:02:41,240 --> 00:02:42,560
I would have done it already.

46
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:45,520
Then what can we do?

47
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:47,720
Let's hire a private detective.

48
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:50,000
Maybe he can find her.

49
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:52,200
I don't feel well.

50
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:55,200
What's wrong, Mom?

51
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:57,080
I have a headache...

52
00:02:57,200 --> 00:02:59,480
Mom is sick, don't provoke her.

53
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:02,960
I have a patient who is a CID.

54
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:07,160
I can ask her to find out if any ID card
was found on the body.

55
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:09,480
If they did, then it wasn't Emma.

56
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:11,360
Great! Don't forget!

57
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:14,240
Don't get ideas in your head.

58
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:15,480
Your sister is smart.

59
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:16,840
She won't get into trouble.

60
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:19,280
Mom is not well. I'll help her upstairs.

61
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:21,840
Come on...

62
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:38,920
I will protect you and Mom

63
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:40,680
and won't get you in trouble.

64
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:43,560
(The day Emma left)

65
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:46,040
Wait...you don't have your old phone,

66
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:47,720
how can I get in touch with you?

67
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:50,160
Get your phone out.

68
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:55,240
This is my new chat app.

69
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:57,280
I'll contact you on my new phone.

70
00:03:57,440 --> 00:03:59,480
Though I lost the old phone,

71
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:01,720
it's OK, Daddy doesn't know the password.

72
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:02,960
He can't turn it on.

73
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:04,560
Remember this icon.

74
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:09,480
Let's use a name Daddy won't suspect.

75
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:11,720
How about... "Louise"?

76
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:14,640
OK! When we book our equestrian classes,

77
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:16,160
we contacted the coach directly.

78
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:18,400
Daddy won't suspect anything.

79
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:20,400
Remember my icon.

80
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:25,400
Don't tell Daddy I have a new phone.

81
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:29,120
If he found out, I couldn't do anything.

82
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:34,920
I'll talk to you when I'm safe.

83
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:38,280
Please don't go.

84
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:41,520
I don't want you to go.

85
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:45,800
I'll contact you, silly.

86
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:50,760
You're not scared out there on your own?

87
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:55,920
This is the first time I'm leaving home.

88
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:59,440
I don't know what the future holds.

89
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:02,040
But that won't stop me...

90
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:04,360
But I'm really scared.

91
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:07,400
Since the day I was born,

92
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:12,080
we have never been apart.

93
00:05:12,880 --> 00:05:16,040
What will happen to me after you're gone?

94
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:19,560
Regardless of how much you hate Daddy,

95
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:22,880
you still have me and Mom.

96
00:05:24,160 --> 00:05:26,880
I'll miss you and Mom too.

97
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:28,560
But I must go.

98
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:32,120
If I don't, I won't know what to do
with my life in the future.

99
00:05:32,280 --> 00:05:37,160
Is what you want really worth
taking the risks?

100
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:40,520
I only know if I don't leave,

101
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:43,080
I'll regret it in the future.

102
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:45,600
You'll understand someday.

103
00:05:45,760 --> 00:05:48,600
No matter what happens,

104
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:50,480
if you're unhappy and you need me,

105
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:52,560
you can always call me.

106
00:05:52,680 --> 00:05:55,520
Wherever I am, I'll always be your sister.

107
00:06:07,840 --> 00:06:09,800
Stop crying!

108
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:14,440
I really must go...

109
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:28,880
Don't blame Elsa.

110
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:34,280
I can't believe she'd run away

111
00:06:34,400 --> 00:06:35,960
and took $1M with her.

112
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:37,280
She's running around with so much cash.

113
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:39,240
And God knows who she's hanging out with.

114
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:41,960
She can't go far without an ID card.

115
00:06:42,080 --> 00:06:44,720
I better go find her.

116
00:06:45,080 --> 00:06:46,760
I'll go with you.

117
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:50,960
I wish I had the nerve to tell Daddy

118
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:52,560
Emma has another phone.

119
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:54,320
If Emma got into an accident,

120
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:56,400
it would have been my fault.

121
00:07:00,280 --> 00:07:01,000
(The night Emma left)

122
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:02,160
What should we do now?

123
00:07:02,320 --> 00:07:05,280
It's dangerous for her to be
out there alone.

124
00:07:05,400 --> 00:07:08,240
We've been to places she usually goes to.

125
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:11,760
It's late. She must have found
a place to stay.

126
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,040
We'll look again tomorrow.

127
00:07:13,160 --> 00:07:14,320
What else can we do?

128
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:17,240
Still no sign of Emma?

129
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:20,600
No. We looked for her all night.

130
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,400
Just now, I tried to turn on her
phone and laptop.

131
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:25,520
They both require a password.

132
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:27,000
Do you know what it is?

133
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:28,280
I don't.

134
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:29,720
Does she have any friends?

135
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:31,600
Anyone she can stay with?

136
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:32,920
I really don't know.

137
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:35,200
Emma didn't say when she left.

138
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:40,560
Who is that? Is it Emma?

139
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:43,760
No...news notification.

140
00:07:44,360 --> 00:07:46,680
You and Emma are very close,

141
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:48,320
she's bound to contact you.

142
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:51,280
You must tell us, OK?

143
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:55,840
I will. I'll get you some ginseng tea.

144
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:04,000
Are you worried Daddy will check my phone?

145
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:05,480
That's why you didn't make contact?

146
00:08:05,680 --> 00:08:08,000
(Day 7 after Emma left)

147
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:10,680
Louise, what happened to you?

148
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:14,160
Hurry up and tell me where you are.

149
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:19,480
Why didn't you contact me?

150
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:21,240
Just call me.

151
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:24,680
If you won't, I'll look for you.

152
00:08:32,800 --> 00:08:34,280
Don't change the subject.

153
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:35,640
Is he your boyfriend?

154
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:36,640
Hey!

155
00:08:36,880 --> 00:08:38,000
Hey!

156
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:39,520
I saw at the bar

157
00:08:39,680 --> 00:08:41,360
you were quite chummy with that guy.

158
00:08:41,720 --> 00:08:43,240
OK! You win.

159
00:08:43,560 --> 00:08:47,240
The guy at the bar...his name is Ken.

160
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:49,600
How did you meet him? Was it romantic?

161
00:08:49,880 --> 00:08:52,240
You're so nosy!

162
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:54,680
Now, you know my biggest secret.

163
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:55,280
Don't you...

164
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:57,280
Don't tell Mom and Daddy, right?

165
00:08:57,400 --> 00:08:58,480
I know.

166
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:00,920
How long do you intend to
keep this from them?

167
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:02,480
I have no idea.

168
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:05,520
Daddy already hit the roof when
he found out I was at a bar.

169
00:09:05,640 --> 00:09:08,120
If he knew I was dating someone, I'm dead.

170
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:09,720
I'll play it by ear.

171
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:10,840
Play by ear?

172
00:09:10,960 --> 00:09:12,840
You're not serious about this guy?

173
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:15,080
Of course not. I'm dead serious.

174
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:17,200
I intend to be with him forever.

175
00:09:17,320 --> 00:09:19,000
You plan to leave home

176
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:21,240
and move in with this guy?

177
00:09:21,280 --> 00:09:22,120
Yes!

178
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:24,480
Is he more important than the family?

179
00:09:24,560 --> 00:09:27,840
Do I have a choice? We have no ID cards.

180
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:30,280
Daddy won't even let us make friends.

181
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:31,920
Let alone date anyone.

182
00:09:32,040 --> 00:09:34,200
Mom and Daddy really love us.

183
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:37,360
At home, we have everything we want.

184
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:39,640
Out there, we'd be on our own.

185
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:42,400
We don't have ID cards, we can't get a job.

186
00:09:42,520 --> 00:09:44,200
You can't do anything without money.

187
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:45,320
What do I have here?

188
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:46,840
Nothing but four walls.

189
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,760
My dream is to venture out

190
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:50,720
and take a look at this world.

191
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:53,360
Meet more people and see more things.

192
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:54,600
After I had my adventure,

193
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:56,000
I'll come back and take you with me

194
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:57,440
so you can see the world too.

195
00:09:57,560 --> 00:10:01,120
OK...out there, you'll get
anything you want.

196
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:02,800
You'll get rich

197
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:05,800
and come back so we can fly anywhere.

198
00:10:05,920 --> 00:10:08,760
You learnt to be sarcastic.

199
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:10,600
When I'm happy flying out there,

200
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:12,240
and be happy with my boyfriend.

201
00:10:12,280 --> 00:10:14,960
Don't be jealous, OK?

202
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:21,680
Emma will definitely contact her boyfriend.

203
00:10:21,760 --> 00:10:22,880
If I can find Ken,

204
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:23,800
I'll be able to find Emma.

205
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:39,040
Emma will definitely contact her boyfriend.

206
00:10:39,160 --> 00:10:40,360
If I can find Ken,

207
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:41,840
I'll be able to find Emma.

208
00:10:46,240 --> 00:10:47,880
Let's try her birthday.

209
00:10:59,120 --> 00:11:02,680
Maybe it's her birthday again.

210
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:07,920
Or the dates in reverse?

211
00:11:09,400 --> 00:11:11,760
Wrong again?

212
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:14,400
Only three more chances left,

213
00:11:14,520 --> 00:11:18,480
If I guessed wrong again,
it'll lock the account.

214
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:31,400
Take the meds and get some rest.

215
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:35,080
Stop thinking. Lie down...

216
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:42,080
Morning, Daddy!

217
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:43,000
Morning!

218
00:11:43,080 --> 00:11:44,120
How is Mom?

219
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:46,920
She didn't sleep well.

220
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:48,640
I just gave her sleeping pills.

221
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:50,280
Let her sleep.

222
00:11:50,880 --> 00:11:52,440
You're not eating breakfast?

223
00:11:52,560 --> 00:11:56,840
No. Keep an eye on Mom, OK?

224
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:10,760
Still no answer.

225
00:12:11,600 --> 00:12:13,440
How can I find Ken?

226
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:19,320
Emma must have used her old phone
to message him before.

227
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:22,680
Where did Daddy hide her phone?

228
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:29,680
Mom? Mom?

229
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:19,480
Thanks!

230
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:30,160
Hey, take your pick.

231
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:32,640
Brother Bo, getting afternoon tea again?

232
00:13:32,720 --> 00:13:36,000
I'm not busy. I love getting afternoon tea.

233
00:13:36,080 --> 00:13:36,800
Ling...
Yes?

234
00:13:36,920 --> 00:13:38,040
The usual for me.
OK!

235
00:13:38,160 --> 00:13:39,480
Let's wait for the team...

236
00:13:39,840 --> 00:13:44,400
Here...two iced lemon water,
easy on the ice and syrup.

237
00:13:44,520 --> 00:13:47,320
Two iced lemon tea,
three iced lemon coffee,

238
00:13:47,440 --> 00:13:49,400
one tea with condensed milk.

239
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:52,360
One corned beef scrambled egg sandwich,
toasted but no edges.

240
00:13:52,480 --> 00:13:53,960
These guys are so picky...

241
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:56,000
How much is it?

242
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:02,600
Brother Bo?

243
00:14:02,720 --> 00:14:03,440
Where are you going?

244
00:14:03,600 --> 00:14:05,120
I got you afternoon tea.

245
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:06,280
I'm on an exchange program.

246
00:14:06,400 --> 00:14:07,680
Upstairs wants my personal details.

247
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:11,320
Sergeant, I'm sorry you had to get
my afternoon tea all the time.

248
00:14:11,480 --> 00:14:13,640
Don't talk like that. I don't mind...

249
00:14:13,800 --> 00:14:16,480
Take a break and you can think.

250
00:14:16,600 --> 00:14:17,480
Hey, take your iced lemon coffee.

251
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:18,400
OK!

252
00:14:18,520 --> 00:14:19,920
Get a straw!
Thanks.

253
00:14:31,960 --> 00:14:32,760
Fung!

254
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:33,480
Ching Sir!

255
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:34,520
What are you working on?

256
00:14:34,800 --> 00:14:36,120
The faceless corpse.

257
00:14:36,760 --> 00:14:40,400
Afternoon tea...come and get it.

258
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:41,360
Perfect!

259
00:14:41,480 --> 00:14:42,480
Come and get it...

260
00:14:42,640 --> 00:14:43,280
Great!

261
00:14:43,400 --> 00:14:45,280
Ching Sir, your iced lemon coffee...

262
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:46,640
Here, Brother Bo...

263
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:48,360
A new case...
Right.

264
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:50,720
Get someone to follow up.
Yes, Sir.

265
00:14:50,840 --> 00:14:52,160
I'll be in a meeting.
Yes, Sir!

266
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:54,960
Pork chop bun...

267
00:14:55,680 --> 00:14:56,840
Ching Sir!

268
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,240
The autopsy report of the faceless
corpse is out.

269
00:14:59,400 --> 00:15:00,360
Thanks.

270
00:15:01,920 --> 00:15:05,520
The report says the victim was between
22 to 25 years old.

271
00:15:05,680 --> 00:15:09,320
The cause of death was internal bleeding
from liver laceration.

272
00:15:09,480 --> 00:15:12,400
The medical examiner deduced she fell
from height.

273
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:14,000
Based on the degree of decomposition,

274
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:17,800
the estimated time of death was
between the 7th and the 10th of this month.

275
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:19,960
Between the 7th and the 10th?

276
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:21,960
That means when she was discovered,

277
00:15:22,080 --> 00:15:23,960
she has been dead three to six days.

278
00:15:24,120 --> 00:15:27,960
A pretty girl chewed up like that
by a wild boar...what a pity!

279
00:15:28,240 --> 00:15:29,960
How do you know she was pretty?

280
00:15:30,080 --> 00:15:32,320
Young girls are usually pretty.

281
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:35,160
A girl in her 20s can't be too ugly.

282
00:15:35,280 --> 00:15:36,480
She was buried.

283
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:38,840
Then it wasn't an accident.

284
00:15:38,960 --> 00:15:40,160
It's probably murder.

285
00:15:40,360 --> 00:15:42,840
You're right. But the key is,

286
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:45,480
the victim didn't have any proof of identity

287
00:15:45,600 --> 00:15:47,960
and her face was chewed up.

288
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:49,800
There's still no match on her fingerprints.

289
00:15:49,920 --> 00:15:52,080
We still don't know who she was.

290
00:15:52,360 --> 00:15:54,480
The girl's outfit was rather trendy.

291
00:15:54,600 --> 00:15:56,280
Looks like she liked to party

292
00:15:56,440 --> 00:15:58,400
and was probably a bar hopper.

293
00:15:58,560 --> 00:15:59,600
Check that out.

294
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:02,480
Brother Bo, there are so many bars
in Hong Kong,

295
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:03,320
where should we start checking?

296
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:05,080
Her clothes are not expensive stuff.

297
00:16:05,160 --> 00:16:06,520
I don't think she has any money.

298
00:16:06,680 --> 00:16:08,200
Start with the cheap ones.

299
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:10,680
Especially those you don't have to pay.

300
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:14,480
Look for bars that have Ladies Night.

301
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:17,200
Those that stamp your arm and give you
free drinks all night.

302
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:20,680
But the report didn't say
there were stamps on her arm.

303
00:16:20,840 --> 00:16:22,480
I'll ask the medical examiner to
double check.

304
00:16:22,600 --> 00:16:25,560
No need. Just go to the morgue.

305
00:16:33,480 --> 00:16:35,280
Thanks. We'll let ourselves out.

306
00:16:35,360 --> 00:16:36,360
OK!

307
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:49,000
Bingo!

308
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:50,800
T Bar...

309
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:18,240
How else can I find Ken?

310
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:22,560
Yes...the bar tender at the bar

311
00:17:22,680 --> 00:17:23,640
seemed quite friendly with Emma.

312
00:17:23,760 --> 00:17:25,160
Maybe he knew Ken.

313
00:17:25,560 --> 00:17:28,480
If I go back to that bar,
maybe I'll find him...

314
00:17:46,080 --> 00:17:47,280
Mom is asleep,

315
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:49,200
Daddy is at work and won't be home soon.

316
00:17:49,280 --> 00:17:51,240
This is the best time to go.

317
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:52,560
I'll go check it out.

318
00:17:58,880 --> 00:18:01,000
Police! Hit the lights and kill the music.

319
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:02,120
Who's in charge?

320
00:18:02,240 --> 00:18:04,240
Bars have undesirable characters
who will attract the Police.

321
00:18:04,360 --> 00:18:05,800
You almost got busted today

322
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:07,160
because you don't have an ID.

323
00:18:08,080 --> 00:18:09,920
The bar is full of undesirable people.

324
00:18:10,040 --> 00:18:11,680
Should I go there alone?

325
00:18:15,040 --> 00:18:17,560
Elsa, haven't seen you at the
library lately.

326
00:18:17,760 --> 00:18:19,440
Even if you don't want to see
the concert with me,

327
00:18:19,560 --> 00:18:22,200
there's no need to stay away from
the library to avoid me.

328
00:18:30,120 --> 00:18:32,760
No. I need a favor.

329
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:35,560
No problem. Call me anytime.

330
00:18:46,400 --> 00:18:48,040
Hello, YY!

331
00:18:48,200 --> 00:18:49,240
Hello, Elsa.

332
00:18:49,440 --> 00:18:51,880
Aren't we going to Tender Bar?

333
00:18:52,040 --> 00:18:54,520
Yes. How should we get there?

334
00:18:54,600 --> 00:18:56,280
Taxi should be the quickest.

335
00:18:56,400 --> 00:18:58,960
No rush. We have time for drinks.

336
00:18:59,080 --> 00:19:00,560
We're not there to drink.

337
00:19:00,680 --> 00:19:01,800
I'm looking for someone.

338
00:19:01,960 --> 00:19:02,960
Looking for someone?

339
00:19:03,360 --> 00:19:04,960
I need to find someone.

340
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:06,720
But I seldom go to bars.

341
00:19:06,840 --> 00:19:09,240
You're a reporter, you've been around.

342
00:19:09,360 --> 00:19:10,960
I'd feel better if you went with me.

343
00:19:11,120 --> 00:19:13,560
No problem. I'll help you any way I can.

344
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:14,680
Let me...

345
00:19:14,800 --> 00:19:17,680
Thanks. I knew I came to the right person.

346
00:19:21,520 --> 00:19:23,560
That's the one. Let's wait for the next one.

347
00:19:23,640 --> 00:19:25,200
No. Let's go...

348
00:19:26,600 --> 00:19:29,400
Wait up...hurry up!

349
00:19:33,560 --> 00:19:34,560
Are you OK?

350
00:19:34,680 --> 00:19:36,520
I'm fine. Thanks.

351
00:19:42,440 --> 00:19:45,000
Who are you looking for? You seem uptight.

352
00:19:47,040 --> 00:19:48,640
Maybe you don't want to tell me.

353
00:19:48,840 --> 00:19:50,560
But if you need my help,

354
00:19:50,680 --> 00:19:51,640
you should at least let me know

355
00:19:51,760 --> 00:19:53,840
who you're looking for so I can help you.

356
00:19:53,960 --> 00:19:56,720
Not that I don't want to tell you.

357
00:19:56,840 --> 00:19:59,800
I just didn't know how.

358
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:02,800
The person I'm looking for,

359
00:20:02,920 --> 00:20:04,040
is my sister's boyfriend.

360
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:05,640
His name is Ken.

361
00:20:05,760 --> 00:20:08,160
But Daddy is against her dating anyone.

362
00:20:08,280 --> 00:20:11,000
I figure if I check out this guy,

363
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:12,640
if he's a nice guy,

364
00:20:12,720 --> 00:20:14,960
I'd help my sister put in
a good word for him.

365
00:20:15,080 --> 00:20:17,800
If he's a creep, I'd tell Emma
to ditch him.

366
00:20:17,920 --> 00:20:21,760
How did you know about Ken and Tender Bar?

367
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:24,600
I don't. But I went with Emma last time.

368
00:20:24,720 --> 00:20:26,600
I saw him there.

369
00:20:26,720 --> 00:20:28,640
I figure he must go there often.

370
00:20:29,160 --> 00:20:31,320
Just ask your sister where Ken is.

371
00:20:31,440 --> 00:20:32,560
I can't do that.

372
00:20:32,720 --> 00:20:35,960
What if he knew I checked up on
her boyfriend secretly?

373
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:38,800
She'd think I'm meddling.

374
00:20:38,920 --> 00:20:41,400
If we don't see Ken at the bar,

375
00:20:41,480 --> 00:20:43,320
ask the bartender for me,

376
00:20:43,400 --> 00:20:46,360
about Ken's background and personality

377
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:47,440
and who does he hang out with.

378
00:20:47,560 --> 00:20:50,160
Don't forget to ask about his hangouts.

379
00:20:51,320 --> 00:20:52,960
I think you should change your name.

380
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:54,400
What?

381
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:56,760
Do you know why my name is YY?

382
00:20:57,440 --> 00:20:59,240
I used to ask a lot of questions
when I was little.

383
00:20:59,320 --> 00:21:00,880
Why, why, why...

384
00:21:00,960 --> 00:21:02,640
That's why my family called me YY.

385
00:21:02,760 --> 00:21:05,080
I guess you can use my name too.

386
00:21:07,160 --> 00:21:07,880
Hey...

387
00:21:07,960 --> 00:21:09,040
Are you OK?

388
00:21:09,080 --> 00:21:10,880
I'm fine. Thanks.

389
00:21:13,120 --> 00:21:15,240
Emma said a true gentleman is rare nowadays.

390
00:21:15,320 --> 00:21:16,840
You seem to be an exception.

391
00:21:17,200 --> 00:21:18,960
No, I charge by the hour.

392
00:21:19,160 --> 00:21:20,880
OK. I'll pay you by day.

393
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:22,520
I can make better use of you.

394
00:21:22,600 --> 00:21:23,440
OK.

395
00:21:33,040 --> 00:21:34,040
What are you doing?

396
00:21:34,320 --> 00:21:35,880
It's clumsy carrying these around.

397
00:21:35,960 --> 00:21:36,840
We'll get them later.

398
00:21:36,960 --> 00:21:37,760
You're right.

399
00:21:53,640 --> 00:21:54,880
You see Ken in here?

400
00:21:55,080 --> 00:21:56,400
Not really...

401
00:21:58,960 --> 00:22:01,200
Two gin tonics.

402
00:22:01,280 --> 00:22:02,080
Sure!

403
00:22:04,800 --> 00:22:05,600
Lee, right?

404
00:22:05,760 --> 00:22:07,480
I'm YY.

405
00:22:07,640 --> 00:22:12,600
I'm looking for Ken. You know him?

406
00:22:12,720 --> 00:22:16,720
Ken? There are a few Kens in here.

407
00:22:16,840 --> 00:22:17,840
Which one are you looking for?

408
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:20,840
This Ken is in his 20s.

409
00:22:20,960 --> 00:22:24,480
Pointed chin and rather skinny.

410
00:22:24,600 --> 00:22:25,960
Not too tall...

411
00:22:26,240 --> 00:22:28,600
Can you stand up...

412
00:22:30,280 --> 00:22:31,840
Shorter than he is.

413
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:35,640
Now, I remember.

414
00:22:35,720 --> 00:22:38,040
This guy is bad news.

415
00:22:38,160 --> 00:22:39,920
He often brings his friends in here.

416
00:22:40,040 --> 00:22:43,600
But they're into different vices.

417
00:22:43,720 --> 00:22:45,200
Really?

418
00:22:45,400 --> 00:22:47,480
Has he been around lately?

419
00:22:47,600 --> 00:22:49,240
What do you want with him?

420
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:52,120
Are you one of his many girlfriends?

421
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:53,760
What do you mean?

422
00:22:53,800 --> 00:22:57,080
People like him always has his arms
around a girl.

423
00:22:57,200 --> 00:22:59,560
Different girls, no less.

424
00:22:59,720 --> 00:23:01,560
Tell your sister to ditch him.

425
00:23:03,360 --> 00:23:05,600
Hi, Crime Unit, New Territories East.

426
00:23:05,720 --> 00:23:07,280
How can I help you, Sir?

427
00:23:07,360 --> 00:23:10,560
Is this the stamp you use for admittance?

428
00:23:10,720 --> 00:23:13,400
Yes, that's the Tender Bar stamp.

429
00:23:13,520 --> 00:23:16,480
Every Thursday night is Ladies Night.

430
00:23:16,560 --> 00:23:17,520
That's the stamp we use.

431
00:23:17,720 --> 00:23:20,960
Can you give us the CCTV footage
from the 1st to the 13th of this month?

432
00:23:21,080 --> 00:23:22,480
Sure. Follow me.

433
00:23:26,800 --> 00:23:28,200
Kwan Sir?

434
00:23:29,280 --> 00:23:32,040
YY the reporter!

435
00:23:32,320 --> 00:23:33,240
You have a good memory.

436
00:23:34,800 --> 00:23:37,360
Please step aside...Police at work.

437
00:23:37,480 --> 00:23:38,600
Excuse me...

438
00:23:38,680 --> 00:23:40,440
Sorry, I'm late. What's the story?

439
00:23:40,560 --> 00:23:42,800
The victim was around 30 years old.

440
00:23:42,920 --> 00:23:44,840
Our initial assessment is that

441
00:23:44,960 --> 00:23:46,360
he killed himself with LPG.

442
00:23:46,480 --> 00:23:48,040
But before he died,

443
00:23:48,160 --> 00:23:50,200
he cut off his genitals with a knife.

444
00:23:50,320 --> 00:23:52,080
Using LPG to commit suicide

445
00:23:52,240 --> 00:23:53,920
needs to plan ahead.

446
00:23:54,120 --> 00:23:57,320
I think he completed some sort of
religious ritual.

447
00:23:57,680 --> 00:23:58,800
Now this officer has good sense.

448
00:23:58,920 --> 00:24:00,160
This should be the Oneness Sect.

449
00:24:00,360 --> 00:24:02,640
What is the Oneness Sect?

450
00:24:02,760 --> 00:24:06,760
It's a hardcore religion from overseas.

451
00:24:06,880 --> 00:24:10,400
They believe suicide is not
the end of your life.

452
00:24:10,520 --> 00:24:12,680
It is a means to put your soul on
a spaceship

453
00:24:12,840 --> 00:24:15,080
and you can embark on a journey
into space.

454
00:24:15,240 --> 00:24:18,800
Male disciples often castrate themselves
before they commit suicide

455
00:24:18,880 --> 00:24:21,640
because they wish to be free from
the constraints of binary gender,

456
00:24:21,760 --> 00:24:23,920
and travel through space in
a genderless state.

457
00:24:24,080 --> 00:24:25,520
You knew about the Oneness Sect.

458
00:24:25,640 --> 00:24:26,760
How could I forget you?

459
00:24:26,880 --> 00:24:28,040
What case are you on?

460
00:24:28,160 --> 00:24:29,640
Haven't you seen the news lately?

461
00:24:29,720 --> 00:24:31,640
The faceless female corpse?

462
00:24:31,760 --> 00:24:32,880
You're so smart.

463
00:24:33,080 --> 00:24:34,400
Do you know her identity?

464
00:24:34,480 --> 00:24:37,400
Nope. Her face was torn up.

465
00:24:37,560 --> 00:24:40,520
No wallet, proof of identity or phone
on the body.

466
00:24:40,600 --> 00:24:41,800
Only a stamp on her arm.

467
00:24:46,720 --> 00:24:47,760
What about fingerprints?

468
00:24:47,920 --> 00:24:50,400
Yes, but we don't have a match.

469
00:24:50,800 --> 00:24:53,600
What are you up to lately?

470
00:24:53,720 --> 00:24:54,960
It must be destiny.

471
00:24:55,120 --> 00:24:56,760
I'm working on this case too.

472
00:24:56,880 --> 00:24:59,400
I'm doing a feature story.

473
00:24:59,520 --> 00:25:02,400
What a coincidence!

474
00:25:02,520 --> 00:25:04,720
If you find anything, let me know.

475
00:25:04,840 --> 00:25:06,800
Of course! We'll swap.

476
00:25:07,600 --> 00:25:08,800
I heard you mention

477
00:25:08,920 --> 00:25:11,360
the girl was here for Ladies Night?

478
00:25:11,480 --> 00:25:12,560
We think so.

479
00:25:12,800 --> 00:25:14,720
That's why we came to see their CCTV

480
00:25:14,800 --> 00:25:17,000
to check for anyone wearing
the victim's clothes

481
00:25:17,120 --> 00:25:19,360
and we'll know what she looked like.

482
00:25:19,440 --> 00:25:22,600
I followed the stamp here.

483
00:25:22,720 --> 00:25:24,440
Why brings you here?

484
00:25:24,640 --> 00:25:26,360
I came with a friend...

485
00:25:26,720 --> 00:25:28,000
to look for someone.

486
00:25:32,720 --> 00:25:35,400
Sorry, YY! You're busy talking,

487
00:25:35,520 --> 00:25:36,480
I need to head home.

488
00:25:36,600 --> 00:25:38,480
I'll let you carry on and I'll get going.

489
00:25:38,640 --> 00:25:39,760
Thank you for your help.

490
00:25:40,600 --> 00:25:42,920
If Emma was the faceless corpse,

491
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:44,880
after she left home

492
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:46,720
did she look for Ken at Tender Bar?

493
00:25:46,800 --> 00:25:49,240
That's why she got a new stamp on her arm?

494
00:25:49,360 --> 00:25:53,640
Oh dear, was Emma really in trouble?

495
00:25:58,520 --> 00:26:00,320
Elsa, I just woke up.

496
00:26:00,400 --> 00:26:02,080
Where are you?

497
00:26:02,560 --> 00:26:04,800
Mom, I went grocery shopping.

498
00:26:04,920 --> 00:26:07,120
I'm on my way home now. See you.

499
00:26:09,880 --> 00:26:11,480
Mom, I'm home!

500
00:26:13,920 --> 00:26:14,960
Daddy?

501
00:26:15,240 --> 00:26:16,600
Elsa, you're back!

502
00:26:17,040 --> 00:26:18,640
When I woke up,

503
00:26:18,760 --> 00:26:20,960
you weren't anywhere in the house.

504
00:26:21,080 --> 00:26:23,080
Have you any idea how worried I was?

505
00:26:23,160 --> 00:26:24,320
Sorry, Mom!

506
00:26:24,480 --> 00:26:26,480
I saw you took sleeping pills,

507
00:26:26,600 --> 00:26:27,800
I know you won't be up soon.

508
00:26:27,880 --> 00:26:30,320
I didn't know Daddy would
come home suddenly.

509
00:26:30,480 --> 00:26:32,400
I went out to Tsimshatsui

510
00:26:32,520 --> 00:26:35,560
and bought special ingredients from
a bigger supermarket

511
00:26:35,640 --> 00:26:37,200
so I can cook for you tonight.

512
00:26:37,760 --> 00:26:39,600
That's far away. What did you get?

513
00:26:39,720 --> 00:26:43,600
Blue cheese pasta with cherry tomatoes

514
00:26:43,680 --> 00:26:45,600
and an avocado salad. What do you think?

515
00:26:45,800 --> 00:26:48,360
Elsa, I'll like anything you make for me.

516
00:26:48,680 --> 00:26:51,480
You really want to make avocado salad?

517
00:26:52,240 --> 00:26:53,440
Yes!

518
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:55,720
You didn't buy avocado.

519
00:26:56,200 --> 00:26:57,880
No avocado?

520
00:27:00,800 --> 00:27:03,520
I'm sure I bought it.

521
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:13,560
It's OK. We'll like anything you make.

522
00:27:17,960 --> 00:27:20,120
You want to ask me something?

523
00:27:20,200 --> 00:27:22,920
You said last time,

524
00:27:23,040 --> 00:27:24,800
you have a patient who's a CID.

525
00:27:24,920 --> 00:27:27,480
Did you find out the identity of
the female corpse?

526
00:27:27,560 --> 00:27:30,120
Of course I did. But she hasn't called back.

527
00:27:30,320 --> 00:27:32,840
You still think it was Emma?

528
00:27:33,320 --> 00:27:37,280
I makes me uneasy when I think about it.

529
00:27:37,360 --> 00:27:39,000
I just want to make sure.

530
00:27:40,880 --> 00:27:41,840
I better start preparing.

531
00:27:42,040 --> 00:27:43,640
I'll call you when the food is ready.

532
00:27:49,840 --> 00:27:51,280
Should I tell Daddy about

533
00:27:51,360 --> 00:27:53,440
what I overheard at the bar?

534
00:27:54,360 --> 00:27:55,520
If I told him,

535
00:27:55,680 --> 00:27:58,400
he's bound to ask how I found out.

536
00:27:58,680 --> 00:27:59,800
Daddy is too smart.

537
00:27:59,920 --> 00:28:02,720
He'll figure out I snuck over
to the bar again

538
00:28:02,880 --> 00:28:07,280
and that Emma has a secret
boyfriend call Ken.

539
00:28:07,440 --> 00:28:08,880
If Emma is alive,

540
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:10,760
she wouldn't want him to know.

541
00:28:11,080 --> 00:28:13,200
In case Emma was the faceless corpse,

542
00:28:13,360 --> 00:28:15,480
and the Police can't find her identity,

543
00:28:15,600 --> 00:28:19,280
if I don't tell Daddy Emma and the faceless
corpse have similar features,

544
00:28:19,400 --> 00:28:22,280
then we'll never know what happened to her.

545
00:28:22,440 --> 00:28:24,360
I better tell Daddy...

546
00:28:28,440 --> 00:28:31,200
(Elsa, I have settled down)

547
00:28:31,320 --> 00:28:32,800
(I'm safe, don't worry)

548
00:28:32,960 --> 00:28:34,320
(I'll be in touch later)

549
00:28:34,480 --> 00:28:36,480
It's Emma!

550
00:28:38,280 --> 00:28:41,680
Daddy, look! Emma said she's safe.

551
00:28:41,880 --> 00:28:43,080
You're sneaky.

552
00:28:43,200 --> 00:28:44,920
You're in touch with Emma all along.

553
00:28:45,040 --> 00:28:46,320
You used the name Louise, right?

554
00:28:46,440 --> 00:28:47,600
But didn't tell us.

555
00:28:47,720 --> 00:28:51,280
Sorry, Daddy! As long as Emma is safe...

556
00:28:51,560 --> 00:28:54,040
Go tell Mom!

557
00:28:54,200 --> 00:28:56,440
Mom should be thrilled.

558
00:28:56,560 --> 00:28:58,040
She'll be able to sleep tonight.

559
00:29:00,240 --> 00:29:03,560
Mom...look!

560
00:29:03,720 --> 00:29:09,120
Emma just texted me she's safe.
She's fine. Don't worry!

561
00:29:10,720 --> 00:29:14,760
It's OK!

562
00:29:18,280 --> 00:29:22,000
Elsa, tell Emma for me

563
00:29:22,120 --> 00:29:25,200
I know she's in touch with you.

564
00:29:25,240 --> 00:29:28,160
If she has decided to leave this family,

565
00:29:28,320 --> 00:29:30,240
there's nothing I can do about it.

566
00:29:30,440 --> 00:29:32,880
I won't look for her either.

567
00:29:33,160 --> 00:29:36,800
She knew she'll break her mother's heart,

568
00:29:36,880 --> 00:29:39,040
but she still went ahead and did it.

569
00:29:39,160 --> 00:29:43,040
Tell her she's on her own from now on.

570
00:29:43,400 --> 00:29:45,000
Do I have to do it?

571
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:47,400
We're cutting her off from now on?

572
00:29:47,560 --> 00:29:50,120
She left us.

573
00:29:51,360 --> 00:29:52,920
Just do it.

574
00:29:53,360 --> 00:29:55,320
I'll pretend I never had
a daughter like her.

575
00:29:55,960 --> 00:30:02,160
You're the only daughter we have
from now on.

576
00:30:12,640 --> 00:30:14,480
OK, I sent it.

577
00:30:17,400 --> 00:30:19,480
I've been thinking...

578
00:30:21,400 --> 00:30:22,560
Now that Emma is gone,

579
00:30:22,640 --> 00:30:24,920
God knows what people she hangs out with.

580
00:30:25,120 --> 00:30:27,080
It's quite dangerous.

581
00:30:27,200 --> 00:30:29,880
She'll eventually get busted.

582
00:30:29,960 --> 00:30:33,640
Then she'll expose you and Mom.

583
00:30:33,720 --> 00:30:37,920
I have decided we should leave
Hong Kong ASAP.

584
00:30:38,040 --> 00:30:40,840
Leave? Where can we go?

585
00:30:40,920 --> 00:30:42,800
You'll know later.

586
00:30:43,080 --> 00:30:44,480
But before we leave,

587
00:30:44,600 --> 00:30:46,760
we must pretend nothing happened.

588
00:30:46,840 --> 00:30:49,600
Don't make anyone suspicious.

589
00:30:49,840 --> 00:30:50,840
If we pack up and leave,

590
00:30:50,960 --> 00:30:52,240
what if Emma wants to come home?

591
00:30:52,360 --> 00:30:54,000
She'll have no home.

592
00:30:54,120 --> 00:30:55,880
I don't think she's coming back.

593
00:30:57,920 --> 00:31:01,160
Elsa, Daddy is right.

594
00:31:01,800 --> 00:31:05,640
We should leave before anything
else happens.

595
00:31:05,760 --> 00:31:08,880
By then, we won't be able to leave.

596
00:31:09,000 --> 00:31:11,120
We might be forced apart.

597
00:31:11,280 --> 00:31:13,720
Elsa, I can't lose you too.

598
00:31:14,840 --> 00:31:17,400
You must come with us.

599
00:31:20,360 --> 00:31:21,520
OK.

600
00:31:29,520 --> 00:31:33,840
Emma, Mom and Daddy are taking me
away from Hong Kong.

601
00:31:33,920 --> 00:31:35,960
I want to see you before I go.

602
00:31:36,040 --> 00:31:38,040
Can you tell me where you are?

603
00:31:38,120 --> 00:31:40,160
I promise I won't tell them.

604
00:31:42,040 --> 00:31:43,360
You won't tell me?

605
00:31:43,560 --> 00:31:44,960
I don't believe you can dodge me.

606
00:31:47,400 --> 00:31:48,680
What's the password?

607
00:31:48,880 --> 00:31:51,200
My birthday and Emma's birthday?

608
00:31:53,160 --> 00:31:55,520
Or the release date of the DSE
we pretended to have taken?

609
00:31:58,480 --> 00:31:59,560
Wrong again!?

610
00:31:59,680 --> 00:32:03,240
Rats! I have one last chance.

611
00:32:03,760 --> 00:32:05,680
Calm down, Hong Ka-yee!

612
00:32:05,800 --> 00:32:07,320
You're close to Emma,

613
00:32:07,440 --> 00:32:09,600
you should know what password she used.

614
00:32:09,720 --> 00:32:12,080
Calm down and think...

615
00:32:12,960 --> 00:32:14,960
OK...I'm in your room now.

616
00:32:15,240 --> 00:32:17,400
Hurry up and leave word for me,

617
00:32:17,480 --> 00:32:19,160
or the limited edition sneakers
will be gone.

618
00:32:19,360 --> 00:32:22,280
It's on, what's the password?

619
00:32:22,400 --> 00:32:24,000
I told you last time,

620
00:32:24,160 --> 00:32:25,680
the day we had our first equestrian lesson.

621
00:32:25,760 --> 00:32:26,960
Do you remember?

622
00:32:27,080 --> 00:32:28,160
Of course I do!

623
00:32:48,560 --> 00:32:50,680
Ken, I found you.

624
00:32:53,240 --> 00:32:54,880
He's in a band as well.

625
00:32:55,000 --> 00:32:57,240
No wonder you guys hit it off.

626
00:32:57,840 --> 00:33:00,960
But so what? You're a scumbag.

627
00:33:01,080 --> 00:33:02,120
When I find Emma,

628
00:33:02,200 --> 00:33:03,640
I'll tell her to ditch Ken.

629
00:33:04,280 --> 00:33:06,680
The key is to persuade Emma to come home.

630
00:33:06,760 --> 00:33:08,640
Then we won't have to leave.

631
00:33:09,680 --> 00:33:14,400
HKIU?

632
00:33:14,960 --> 00:33:16,800
YY went to school there.

633
00:33:17,480 --> 00:33:18,720
Better ask him for help...

634
00:33:18,840 --> 00:33:20,520
If you find anything, let me know.

635
00:33:20,680 --> 00:33:22,200
I'm working on this case too.

636
00:33:22,360 --> 00:33:25,120
I'm doing a feature story.

637
00:33:26,240 --> 00:33:31,440
What if YY found out about me?

638
00:33:31,560 --> 00:33:33,120
He's chummy with the Police.

639
00:33:33,200 --> 00:33:34,720
I'll be asking for trouble.

640
00:33:34,840 --> 00:33:37,280
Forget it. I'll go by myself.

641
00:33:51,080 --> 00:33:53,120
Excuse me...do you know

642
00:33:53,240 --> 00:33:55,720
where can I find people in a band?

643
00:33:55,840 --> 00:33:58,120
You want the band room?

644
00:33:58,240 --> 00:34:01,400
Take these stairs to the West Wing.

645
00:34:01,560 --> 00:34:05,040
I want that...

646
00:34:05,400 --> 00:34:06,800
Want what?

647
00:34:07,080 --> 00:34:08,560
I'm browsing through Instabook

648
00:34:08,680 --> 00:34:11,680
and saw a Joint U Live Band Party.

649
00:34:11,800 --> 00:34:13,640
They said the legendary Band Stud

650
00:34:13,760 --> 00:34:16,200
will be there to jam music.

651
00:34:16,280 --> 00:34:17,800
If I were in the university,

652
00:34:17,920 --> 00:34:19,760
I could have played a song or two with him.

653
00:34:19,920 --> 00:34:22,480
Then I can die with no regrets.

654
00:34:22,960 --> 00:34:24,960
I hope you'll get your chance.

655
00:34:28,680 --> 00:34:29,840
This is Dr. Hong.

656
00:34:30,280 --> 00:34:32,240
Dr. Hong, two officers from the
New Territories East Crime Unit

657
00:34:32,360 --> 00:34:34,400
are waiting downstairs to see you.

658
00:34:36,400 --> 00:34:38,400
No problem. Send them up.

659
00:34:38,560 --> 00:34:40,160
Yes, Dr. Hong.

660
00:34:49,440 --> 00:34:50,400
Come in!

661
00:34:51,480 --> 00:34:56,320
Dr. Hong, these are the officers from
the New Territories East Crime Unit.

662
00:34:56,400 --> 00:34:57,360
Please have a seat.

663
00:34:57,440 --> 00:34:58,600
This way...

664
00:35:02,360 --> 00:35:03,440
Hello, Dr. Hong.

665
00:35:03,800 --> 00:35:06,400
I'm Kwan Zhi-fung of the New Territories
East Crime Unit.

666
00:35:06,800 --> 00:35:08,520
I'm Lee Shun-cheong.

667
00:35:09,040 --> 00:35:11,040
What can I do for you, officers?

668
00:35:11,400 --> 00:35:13,800
Dr. Hong, we came to ask you

669
00:35:13,880 --> 00:35:17,480
about endometriosis or what is
commonly known as chocolate cyst.

670
00:35:17,560 --> 00:35:20,120
We're tracing an oral drug for
chocolate cyst.

671
00:35:20,280 --> 00:35:21,600
This is the one.

672
00:35:22,680 --> 00:35:25,000
We understand this is a new drug
made in Hong Kong

673
00:35:25,080 --> 00:35:27,880
and must be prescribed by
obstetricians and gynecologists.

674
00:35:28,000 --> 00:35:29,960
That's why we wanted to know

675
00:35:30,080 --> 00:35:35,000
how often is this drug prescribed?

676
00:35:35,160 --> 00:35:36,800
Here...got it.

677
00:35:36,920 --> 00:35:39,880
Obstetricians and gynecologists of
this hospital, including me,

678
00:35:39,960 --> 00:35:41,080
over the past six months,

679
00:35:41,200 --> 00:35:44,600
have prescribed this drug to 33 patients.

680
00:35:44,720 --> 00:35:48,280
Can I ask you why you need this information?

681
00:35:48,640 --> 00:35:50,200
It's about a case we're working on.

682
00:35:50,320 --> 00:35:52,040
The recent faceless female corpse.

683
00:35:56,800 --> 00:35:59,560
The autopsy report showed the victim

684
00:35:59,680 --> 00:36:01,720
had a chocolate cyst on the left side
of the pelvic peritoneum.

685
00:36:01,800 --> 00:36:04,240
We found traces of this drug in her blood.

686
00:36:04,320 --> 00:36:07,080
Since there was no proof of identity
on the body,

687
00:36:07,200 --> 00:36:10,320
we're trying to trace the drug.

688
00:36:10,400 --> 00:36:12,760
Dr. Hong, do you remember

689
00:36:12,880 --> 00:36:15,800
prescribing this drug to a patient

690
00:36:15,920 --> 00:36:17,720
who matches the figure of the body?

691
00:36:18,200 --> 00:36:24,040
I might need to read the autopsy report

692
00:36:24,160 --> 00:36:26,000
before I can answer your question.

693
00:36:26,240 --> 00:36:29,160
Can you give us a list of the patients

694
00:36:29,280 --> 00:36:30,600
who have taken this drug?

695
00:36:30,760 --> 00:36:34,600
Sorry, because it involves
the patients' privacy,

696
00:36:34,720 --> 00:36:37,000
the hospital must reach a consensus

697
00:36:37,080 --> 00:36:39,800
before we can respond to your request.

698
00:36:39,920 --> 00:36:42,480
We understand. We'll wait to hear from you.

699
00:36:42,680 --> 00:36:43,480
No problem.

700
00:36:43,600 --> 00:36:45,920
Dr. Hong, we'll excuse ourselves.

701
00:36:46,040 --> 00:36:46,760
Thank you.

702
00:36:46,880 --> 00:36:47,920
Please come this way.

703
00:36:57,240 --> 00:36:57,800
Here...drink some warm water.

704
00:36:57,920 --> 00:36:58,640
See if it'll help.

705
00:36:58,760 --> 00:37:00,320
Emma, hang in there.

706
00:37:00,440 --> 00:37:02,840
Daddy is on his way home.

707
00:37:04,880 --> 00:37:06,240
Emma, how are you?

708
00:37:06,360 --> 00:37:07,400
Daddy brought a new drug.

709
00:37:07,480 --> 00:37:09,480
Take it and you'll feel better.

710
00:37:10,880 --> 00:37:12,320
Water, Emma.

711
00:37:36,640 --> 00:37:39,640
The autopsy report showed the victim

712
00:37:39,760 --> 00:37:41,920
has a chocolate cyst on the left side
of the pelvic peritoneum.

713
00:37:42,040 --> 00:37:44,400
We found traces of this drug in her blood.

714
00:37:44,480 --> 00:37:47,520
Since there was no proof of identity
on the body...

715
00:38:02,960 --> 00:38:04,920
Hello! Are you Ken?

716
00:38:05,000 --> 00:38:06,360
Yes. You are...

717
00:38:06,480 --> 00:38:07,760
I'm Emma's sister.

718
00:38:07,880 --> 00:38:08,640
Emma's sister?

719
00:38:08,840 --> 00:38:10,440
You're Emma Hong's boyfriend,

720
00:38:10,560 --> 00:38:11,960
your name is Ken, right?

721
00:38:12,040 --> 00:38:13,880
Yes...what is it?

722
00:38:14,000 --> 00:38:15,240
I just knew it.

723
00:38:15,360 --> 00:38:17,440
I recognized you from the bar last time.

724
00:38:17,560 --> 00:38:19,000
Emma ran away from home,

725
00:38:19,080 --> 00:38:20,200
that's why you came to see me?

726
00:38:20,320 --> 00:38:22,080
Do you know where she is?

727
00:38:22,200 --> 00:38:23,760
I really want to see her.

728
00:38:23,880 --> 00:38:25,520
Relax! She's in a safe place.

729
00:38:25,640 --> 00:38:26,480
I'll take you to her now.

730
00:38:26,600 --> 00:38:27,640
Great! Thanks!

731
00:38:27,760 --> 00:38:28,640
This way...

732
00:38:36,560 --> 00:38:38,840
Where are you now?

733
00:38:44,600 --> 00:38:45,480
Fung Sir!

734
00:38:45,800 --> 00:38:48,240
We have the result from
the fingerprints database.

735
00:38:48,360 --> 00:38:50,360
Nothing matched the corpse.

736
00:38:50,480 --> 00:38:52,080
We also have the DNA report.

737
00:38:52,160 --> 00:38:54,040
No match either.

738
00:38:54,120 --> 00:38:57,720
It's likely she was an illegal immigrant.

739
00:38:58,280 --> 00:39:02,960
I saw the patient list from Dr. Hong.

740
00:39:03,040 --> 00:39:05,040
Nothing there either.

741
00:39:05,160 --> 00:39:08,240
That's odd. How could an II have access to

742
00:39:08,320 --> 00:39:11,160
a drug prescribed by obstetricians
and gynecologists?

743
00:39:11,240 --> 00:39:13,720
Did she know a doctor who could
pull some strings?

744
00:39:13,840 --> 00:39:14,880
Or she stole them?

745
00:39:15,000 --> 00:39:17,000
Even when there's no match on DNA
or fingerprints,

746
00:39:17,080 --> 00:39:18,720
it doesn't mean she's an II.

747
00:39:18,840 --> 00:39:20,600
Probably someone without an ID card

748
00:39:20,720 --> 00:39:23,640
but somehow managed to live in Hong Kong

749
00:39:23,720 --> 00:39:26,840
such as an overstayer or illegal resident.

750
00:39:26,960 --> 00:39:31,400
We just don't know how she managed
to have access to this drug.

751
00:39:31,520 --> 00:39:34,440
Let's check places where people with
no ID cards usually hang out.

752
00:39:34,520 --> 00:39:39,120
Let's start with brothels
and illegal guest houses.

753
00:39:43,000 --> 00:39:44,200
Here we are!

754
00:39:49,520 --> 00:39:50,000
Come on in...

755
00:39:50,080 --> 00:39:50,840
Thanks.

756
00:39:50,920 --> 00:39:53,880
Emma...

757
00:39:56,680 --> 00:39:58,200
Where's Emma?

758
00:39:58,680 --> 00:40:00,240
You can't be that naive!

759
00:40:00,440 --> 00:40:02,920
What are you doing? Stay back!

760
00:40:04,480 --> 00:40:06,400
Stay back...

761
00:40:20,400 --> 00:40:22,920
Give it back to me, you creep!

762
00:40:23,000 --> 00:40:26,280
Elsa, I'll be home early tonight.

763
00:40:26,880 --> 00:40:28,200
When Mom wakes up,

764
00:40:28,280 --> 00:40:34,400
tell her I have something important
to discuss with you tonight.

765
00:40:34,440 --> 00:40:37,440
Let go of me...

766
00:40:43,840 --> 00:40:44,880
Hello, Elsa?

767
00:40:45,000 --> 00:40:46,200
Are you Elsa's father?

768
00:40:48,560 --> 00:40:50,080
Yes. Who are you?

769
00:40:50,200 --> 00:40:52,680
Want to hear your precious daughter's voice?

770
00:40:52,760 --> 00:40:54,840
Help...Daddy, help me...

771
00:40:55,000 --> 00:40:57,200
Elsa! Elsa, what's wrong?

772
00:40:57,240 --> 00:40:58,520
Where are you, Elsa?

773
00:40:58,600 --> 00:41:02,080
Listen, I want $3M, all in $500 notes.

774
00:41:02,160 --> 00:41:03,480
Before 6 o'clock tonight,

775
00:41:03,560 --> 00:41:05,760
put it next to the garbage can in
the Lok Ping Road park.

776
00:41:05,880 --> 00:41:07,920
No Police. Or you know what will happen.

777
00:41:08,000 --> 00:41:11,000
OK...I'll pay you. Don't hurt Elsa.

778
00:41:11,160 --> 00:41:14,880
Good! No games or you'll never
see her again.

779
00:41:15,880 --> 00:41:17,680
Hello? Hello?

780
00:41:22,200 --> 00:41:23,480
Sir, can I help you?

781
00:41:23,600 --> 00:41:25,040
I wish to withdraw $3M cash.

782
00:41:25,200 --> 00:41:26,640
All in $500 notes.

783
00:41:26,800 --> 00:41:28,480
Did you call in advance?

784
00:41:28,600 --> 00:41:29,440
No.

785
00:41:29,520 --> 00:41:31,240
Sorry, if you didn't call ahead,

786
00:41:31,320 --> 00:41:34,600
we don't have that much cash ready.

787
00:41:34,680 --> 00:41:37,040
I'll take as much as you have.

788
00:41:41,200 --> 00:41:42,400
All set, Mr. Hong.

789
00:41:42,520 --> 00:41:43,600
Thank you.

790
00:41:45,760 --> 00:41:47,480
I just called ahead

791
00:41:47,600 --> 00:41:49,520
to meet with your manager, Mr. Chan.

792
00:41:51,280 --> 00:41:53,520
Mr. Hong, here's $500K.

793
00:41:53,640 --> 00:41:54,880
Thank you.
Sure!

794
00:42:13,960 --> 00:42:16,760
Relax! We'll go to Meow Lung Kee
in a few days

795
00:42:16,880 --> 00:42:18,400
and we're all set.

796
00:42:18,560 --> 00:42:21,360
But I have things to do right now.

797
00:42:21,760 --> 00:42:22,760
Later.

798
00:42:23,000 --> 00:42:27,360
Let go of me...

799
00:42:28,120 --> 00:42:30,760
Don't worry, your rich Daddy will save you.

800
00:42:31,000 --> 00:42:33,240
What have you done to Emma? Where is she?

801
00:42:33,400 --> 00:42:34,840
You said I'm her boyfriend,

802
00:42:34,960 --> 00:42:36,360
what do you think?

803
00:42:36,600 --> 00:42:44,680
Let go of me...
